# Ignore PyTorch model files
*.pt
*.pth

# Extras
ixi_nd.ipynb
ixi_last.ipynb
mt.ipynb
registration.py
simc.ipynb
spat_v_spect.ipynb
unet_comp.ipynb
zvit.ipynb

# Launch scripts and docs live in `/spectralvit_kb/jobs`, not the repo
*.sbatch
slurm/

# Covariates
docs/
# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Experiment outputs
results/
# Datasets and caches: MedMNIST npz, the CIFAR batches, anything a sweep downloads or
# stages. These belong on spacelink, not in the repo; data/ is only ever a staging point.
data/
hcp_age_bak.txt
dbs_3d/verify_5tests.ipynb
dbs_3d/metrics_table.*

# Recovered from /checkpoints/zip/manuscript.zip, not repo content
paper/
# Exception, force-added once and so tracked from here on: every manuscript figure has
# to rebuild from a repo script against these inputs, which is not possible if they are
# only ever in /tmp. A tracked path ignores the rule above, so no negation is needed.
#   paper/cvpr/fig/data/
# Participant-level tables. hca_ages_raw.tsv and participants_hca.tsv are HCP-Aging
# subject IDs with ages, which the NIMH Data Archive DUC does not permit redistributing,
# and this repo is public. They belong on spacelink with the cohort data.
*.tsv
# SLURM stdout dropped in the repo root by jobs run from here, and the .bak* snapshots the
# sweeps leave when a config is swapped. Both are working residue: ~45 and ~25 files that
# otherwise bury git status and sit one `git add -A` away from being committed.
slurm-*.out
*.bak*
